   people. Your copy, and any changes you make to it, stay yours alone
   (Section 4). The only way to get a change to anyone else is a pull
   request to the Owner's repository (Section 6).

2. What this license covers

   Everything in the Software is covered, not only the code:

   a. the source code and every compiled, built or hosted form of it;
   b. the visual design: the layouts, screens, components, page structure
      and overall look and feel of the app, its landing page and its other
      pages;
   c. the theme system: the design tokens, colour palettes and accent
      presets, typography choices and scales, spacing, corner, shadow and
      motion rules, and the stylesheets and styled components that apply
      them;
   d. the assets: the Chronicles name and logo, icons and app icons,
      illustrations, screenshots, the Owner's own photographs, the
      headline artwork, and the written copy and documentation.

   The rights in Sections 1 and 6 apply to all of it. The restrictions in
   Sections 3 and 4 apply to all of it, whether it is copied directly or
   closely recreated.

