6. Contributions: pull requests and issues

   a. Pull requests. You may fork the repository on GitHub to prepare a
      pull request to the Owner's repository, and you may keep using your
      changes on your own devices for your own personal use (Section 1).
      You may not publish or distribute a changed version, or use it for
      anyone but yourself: changes reach other people only through a pull
      request that the Owner merges into the Owner's repository. The Owner
      may accept, change, decline or close any pull request without giving
      a reason.

   b. Issues. You may report bugs and suggest features through the
      repository's issue tracker, or through the "Feedback/Report a Bug"
      form in the Software. Issues are public: do not include passwords,
      recovery keys, health information or other personal data. Report
      security problems privately to support@mydailychronicles.com, not in
      an issue.

   c. Rights in contributions. By submitting a pull request, issue,
      suggestion or other contribution, you confirm that it is your own work
      (or that you have the right to submit it) and you grant the Owner a
      perpetual, worldwide, irrevocable, royalty-free license to use, copy,
      modify, distribute, sublicense and relicense it, as part of the
      Software or otherwise, without payment or obligation to you. A merged
      contribution becomes part of the Software under this license.

   Contributing does not give you any further right to use the Software:
   use stays limited to Section 1.

